# F — Correlation / redundancy analysis

Accuracy alone is not sufficient.

Measure prediction agreement/correlation between candidates.

Specifically identify cases where several indicators are effectively the same information expressed differently.

Examples:

* EMA / MA / SuperTrend / HOTT / MavilimW may all represent trend.
* RSI / WaveTrend / MACD may share momentum information.
* Several Q-learning variants may produce highly similar forecasts.

Do not allow ten correlated models to count as ten independent votes.

Produce a correlation/agreement matrix and cluster components into information families.

Report:

* highly redundant components,
* genuinely independent predictors,
* components whose forecasts are negatively correlated,
* components that appear directionally inverted.

